/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - A transit (vernier) theodolite is built round four lines.
   - The least count of a vernier is the value of one main-scale division divided by the number of vernier divisions.
   - Face left means the vertical circle is on the observer's left when sighting; face right, on the right.
   - Centring is checked again after levelling, because levelling moves the head slightly.
   - For a correct theodolite: (1) the plate level axis is perpendicular to the vertical axis; (2) the vertical cross-hair lies in a plane perpendicular to the horizontal axis; (3) the line of collimation is perpendicular to the horizontal axis;
*/
